From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ysfaculty <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:54:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 184/194] hjviewer: no stray 1 before Korean typed after
 deleting the PC's text
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On an iPhone with the Korean keyboard, after deleting text that was already
on the PC's line (a command recalled in PuTTY) with the keyboard's
Backspace, the Korean typed next arrived with a "1" in front of it.

The hidden field starts as 1024 filler characters ('1', initText in
remote_page.dart). Text the PC already had is not in the field, so each
Backspace on it deletes a filler character and the field becomes a shorter
filler with no typed text. The Korean keyboard can put one filler character
back before the next syllable (rustdesk PR #15201's "over-restored
sentinel"). iosSoftKeyboardEdit (flutter/lib/models/soft_keyboard_input.dart)
dropped that character only on a full filler (oldFiller ==
initialFillerLength); on the shortened one the diff sent the restored '1'
and then the syllable.

The guard now applies whenever the old field is filler only, full or
shortened: filler characters that appear right before Hangul, with nothing
else after them, are not typed. A 1 the user types is still sent: alone or
several (11), followed by other text (1a), after typed text (가1), and while
the keyboard composes (the old condition). On an iPhone, typing a 1 and
then Hangul takes a layout switch, so typed keys never bring them in one
settled edit; once the 1 has been sent, a filler character put back before
the next syllable is dropped as above and the 1 stays.

Left alone: the keyboard's Backspace that removes a filler character and
puts it back within one settled edit still sends nothing. Resetting the
field on such an edit was considered, but no device log shows that
sequence, and a reset between the keyboard's steps could send the
restored character or drop a key; the key bar's Backspace (previous patch)
covers it.

Tests: the reported sequence (two Backspaces on the PC's text, then a
syllable with one restored 1: no 1 sent, and the 1.9.3 guard sent it), a
restored 1 or two on a shortened filler, typed 1s on a full and a shortened
filler, alone and after Hangul, and the existing cases unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
